<hr>##x000A;</div>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="25:1-25:100" dir="auto">Welcome to OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin), a platform for software development agents 
powered by AI.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="27:1-28:64" dir="auto">OpenHands agents can do anything a human developer can: modify code, run commands, 
browse the web,##x000A;call APIs, and yes—even copy code snippets from StackOverflow.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="30:1-30:108" dir="auto">Learn more at 
<a data-sourcepos="30:15-30:62" href="https://docs.all-hands.dev" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">docs.all-hands.dev</a>, or jump to the
<a data-sourcepos="30:80-30:107" href="#-quick-start">Quick Start</a>.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="32:1-32:51" dir="auto"><a class="no-attachment-icon 
gfm" href="/root/openhands/-/raw/main/docs/static/img/screenshot.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img data-sourcepos="32:1-32:51" 
src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAAAACH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw==" alt="App screenshot" decoding="async" class="lazy gfm" 
data-src="/root/openhands/-/raw/main/docs/static/img/screenshot.png"></a></p>##x000A;<h2 data-sourcepos="34:1-34:18" dir="auto">##x000A;<a 
href="#-quick-start" aria-hidden="true" class="anchor" id="user-content--quick-start"></a><gl-emoji title="high voltage sign" data-name="zap" 
data-unicode-version="4.0">⚡</gl-emoji> Quick Start</h2>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="36:1-37:59" dir="auto">The easiest way to run OpenHands is in Docker. 
You can change <code data-sourcepos="36:64-36:77">WORKSPACE_BASE</code> below to##x000A;point OpenHands to existing code that you'd like to 
modify.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="39:1-40:41" dir="auto">See the <a data-sourcepos="39:9-39:83" 
href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Getting Started</a> guide 
for##x000A;system requirements and more information.</p>##x000A;<div class="gl-relative markdown-code-block js-markdown-code">##x000A;<pre 
data-sourcepos="42:1-57:3" data-canonical-lang="bash" class="code highlight js-syntax-highlight language-shell" v-pre="true"><code><span id="LC1" 
class="line" lang="shell"><span class="nb">export </span><span class="nv">WORKSPACE_BASE</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="si">$(</span><span 
class="nb">pwd</span><span class="si">)</span>/workspace</span>##x000A;<span id="LC2" class="line" lang="shell"></span>##x000A;<span id="LC3" class="line" 
lang="shell">docker pull ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik</span>##x000A;<span id="LC4" class="line" lang="shell"></span>##x000A;<span id="LC5" 
class="line" lang="shell">docker run <span class="nt">-it</span> <span class="nt">--pull</span><span class="o">=</span>always <span 
class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC6" class="line" lang="shell">    <span class="nt">-e</span> <span 
class="nv">SANDBOX_RUNTIME_CONTAINER_IMAGE</span><span class="o">=</span>ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik <span 
class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC7" class="line" lang="shell">    <span class="nt">-e</span> <span class="nv">SANDBOX_USER_ID</span><span 
class="o">=</span><span class="si">$(</span><span class="nb">id</span> <span class="nt">-u</span><span class="si">)</span> <span 
class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC8" class="line" lang="shell">    <span class="nt">-e</span> <span class="nv">WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH</span><span
class="o">=</span><span class="nv">$WORKSPACE_BASE</span> <span class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC9" class="line" lang="shell">    <span 
class="nt">-v</span> <span class="nv">$WORKSPACE_BASE</span>:/opt/workspace_base <span class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC10" class="line" 
lang="shell">    <span class="nt">-v</span> /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock <span class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC11" class="line" 
lang="shell">    <span class="nt">-p</span> 3000:3000 <span class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC12" class="line" lang="shell">    <span 
class="nt">--add-host</span> host.docker.internal:host-gateway <span class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC13" class="line" lang="shell">    <span 
class="nt">--name</span> openhands-app-<span class="si">$(</span><span class="nb">date</span> +%Y%m%d%H%M%S<span class="si">)</span> <span 
class="se">\</span></span>##x000A;<span id="LC14" class="line" lang="shell">    
ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/openhands:0.9</span></code></pre>##x000A;<copy-code></copy-code><insert-code-snippet></insert-code-snippet>##x000A;</div>##x000A;<p 
data-sourcepos="59:1-59:80" dir="auto">You'll find OpenHands running at <a data-sourcepos="59:34-59:79" href="http://localhost:3000" rel="nofollow 
noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">http://localhost:3000</a>!</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="61:1-61:197" dir="auto">You'll need a model provider and API 
key. One option that works well: <a data-sourcepos="61:71-61:120" href="https://www.anthropic.com/api" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" 
target="_blank">Claude 3.5 Sonnet</a>, but you have <a data-sourcepos="61:136-61:196" href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/llms" rel="nofollow 
noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">many options</a>.</p>##x000A;<hr data-sourcepos="63:1-64:0">##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="65:1-66:85" dir="auto">You can 
also run OpenHands in a scriptable <a data-sourcepos="65:44-65:121" href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/headless-mode" rel="nofollow 
noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">headless mode</a>,##x000A;or as an <a data-sourcepos="66:10-66:84" 
href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/cli-mode" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">interactive CLI</a>.</p>##x000A;<p 
data-sourcepos="68:1-68:126" dir="auto">Visit <a data-sourcepos="68:7-68:81" href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started" rel="nofollow 
noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Getting Started</a> for more information and setup instructions.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="70:1-70:144" 
dir="auto">If you want to modify the OpenHands source code, check out <a data-sourcepos="70:60-70:143" 
href="https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" 
target="_blank">Development.md</a>.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="72:1-72:110" dir="auto">Having issues? The <a data-sourcepos="72:20-72:100" 
href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/troubleshooting" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Troubleshooting Guide</a> can 
help.</p>##x000A;<h2 data-sourcepos="74:1-74:21" dir="auto">##x000A;<a href="#-documentation" aria-hidden="true" class="anchor" 
id="user-content--documentation"></a><gl-emoji title="open book" data-name="book" data-unicode-version="6.0">📖</gl-emoji> Documentation</h2>##x000A;<p 
data-sourcepos="76:1-77:92" dir="auto">To learn more about the project, and for tips on using OpenHands,##x000A;<strong data-sourcepos="77:1-77:91">check 
out our <a data-sourcepos="77:17-77:89" href="https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" 
target="_blank">documentation</a></strong>.</p>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="79:1-80:62" dir="auto">There you'll find resources on how to use different LLM 
providers,##x000A;troubleshooting resources, and advanced configuration options.</p>##x000A;<h2 data-sourcepos="82:1-82:25" dir="auto">##x000A;<a 
href="#-how-to-contribute" aria-hidden="true" class="anchor" id="user-content--how-to-contribute"></a><gl-emoji title="handshake" data-name="handshake" 
data-unicode-version="9.0">🤝</gl-emoji> How to Contribute</h2>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="84:1-86:66" dir="auto">OpenHands is a community-driven project, 
and we welcome contributions from everyone.##x000A;Whether you're a developer, a researcher, or simply enthusiastic about advancing the field 
of##x000A;software engineering with AI, there are many ways to get involved:</p>##x000A;<ul data-sourcepos="88:1-91:0" dir="auto">##x000A;<li 
data-sourcepos="88:1-88:133">##x000A;<strong data-sourcepos="88:3-88:25">Code Contributions:</strong> Help us develop new agents, core functionality, the 
frontend and other interfaces, or sandboxing solutions.</li>##x000A;<li data-sourcepos="89:1-89:158">##x000A;<strong data-sourcepos="89:3-89:30">Research 
and Evaluation:</strong> Contribute to our understanding of LLMs in software engineering, participate in evaluating the models, or suggest 
improvements.</li>##x000A;<li data-sourcepos="90:1-91:0">##x000A;<strong data-sourcepos="90:3-90:27">Feedback and Testing:</strong> Use the OpenHands 
toolset, report bugs, suggest features, or provide feedback on usability.</li>##x000A;</ul>##x000A;<p data-sourcepos="92:1-92:63" dir="auto">For details, 
please check <a data-sourcepos="92:27-92:62" href="/root/openhands/-/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" class="gfm">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</p>##x000A;<h2 
data-sourcepos="94:1-94:26" dir="auto">##x000A;<a href="#-join-our-community" aria-hidden="true" class="anchor" 
id="user-content--join-our-community"></a><gl-emoji title="robot face" data-name="robot" data-unicode-version="8.0">🤖</gl-emoji> Join Our 
