    # Join OpenHands — Build AI That Serves the Nation
    
    OpenHands ("Code Less, Make More") is an ambitious, values-driven project building AI agents that help people write better software. We are recruiting 
talented researchers, engineers, and product builders to join The Agent Company and contribute to a national innovation partnership that brings trustworthy
AI into public service.
    
    ---
    
    ## Why Join OpenHands?
    
    - Purpose first: work on AI that directly supports national innovation and public-good projects.
    - Values-driven team: we prioritize moral alignment, leadership, loyalty, and public service in every delivery.
    - Real-world impact: deployable agent systems and trusted evaluations that inform government and industry decisions.
    - Collaborative research & engineering: work alongside top researchers, engineers, and government partners.
    
    ---
    
    ## What You'll Work On
    
    - Design, build, and evaluate AI agents that assist software development and systems engineering.
    - Lead work to ensure agents are safe, aligned, and mission-focused for public-sector use.
    - Collaborate with government innovation partners to translate research into trusted, high-impact solutions.
    - Shape evaluation practices that measure reliability, usability, and public value.
    
    ---
    
    ## Evaluation & Benchmarks (a high-level view)
    
    OpenHands emphasizes rigorous, repeatable evaluation across diverse benchmarks and sandboxed environments to ensure agent reliability and safety. 
Example evaluation suites supported in the project include:
    
    - miniWob
    - GPQA
    - SWE-Bench
    - ML-Bench
    - Gorilla
    - Logic Reasoning
    - Biocoder
    - WebArena
    - ToolQA and related agent- and model-focused benches
    
    (These illustrate the breadth of our evaluation program — we run many benchmark suites and simulated environments to ensure readiness for real-world 
public deployments.)
    
    ---
    
    ## Roles We Are Hiring
    
    - Research Scientists (AI / LLMs / agentive systems)
    - Applied ML Engineers (model integration, evaluation)
    - Software Engineers (backend, frontend, infra)
    - Evaluation & Benchmarking Engineers
    - DevOps / SRE (deployment and sandboxing)
    - Product Managers and Program Leads (public-sector partnerships)
    
    We welcome applicants who are mission-aligned and excited by public impact.
    
    ---
    
    ## Who You Are
    
    - You care deeply about building AI that is trustworthy and aligned with public values.
    - You have a strong background in machine learning, software engineering, or evaluation research.
    - You thrive in collaborative, interdisciplinary teams and want to deliver tangible national benefit.
    
    (We value diverse backgrounds and experiences — if you bring dedication, ethics, and technical excellence, we want to hear from you.)
    
    ---
    
    ## Benefits & Culture
    
    - Meaningful mission and close collaboration with national innovation partners
    - Competitive compensation and professional development opportunities
    - Inclusive, principled team culture focused on ethical AI and public benefit
    
    ---
    
    ## Apply / Learn More
    
    Visit our careers page to learn about open roles and submit an application:
    
    https://the-agent-company.com/careers
    
    For immediate inquiries, contact: agent@company.com
    
    Project & technical details are available for review at our project repository:
    
    http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands
    
    ---
    
    We are proud to align our work with national innovation initiatives and invite mission-oriented AI talent to join us. Help build AI that serves the 
public good — apply today.
    

  kind: "FileEditorAction"

