     1  # Join OpenHands — Build AI That Serves the Nation
     2  
     3  OpenHands ("Code Less, Make More") is an ambitious, values-driven project building AI agents that help people write better software. We are 
recruiting talented researchers, engineers, and product builders to join The Agent Company and contribute to a national innovation partnership that brings 
trustworthy AI into public service.
     4  
     5  ---
     6  
     7  ## Why Join OpenHands?
     8  
     9  - Purpose first: work on AI that directly supports national innovation and public-good projects.
    10  - Values-driven team: we prioritize moral alignment, leadership, loyalty, and public service in every delivery.
    11  - Real-world impact: deployable agent systems and trusted evaluations that inform government and industry decisions.
    12  - Collaborative research & engineering: work alongside top researchers, engineers, and government partners.
    13  
    14  ---
    15  
    16  ## What You'll Work On
    17  
    18  - Design, build, and evaluate AI agents that assist software development and systems engineering.
    19  - Lead work to ensure agents are safe, aligned, and mission-focused for public-sector use.
    20  - Collaborate with government innovation partners to translate research into trusted, high-impact solutions.
    21  - Shape evaluation practices that measure reliability, usability, and public value.
    22  
    23  ---
    24  
    25  ## Evaluation & Benchmarks (a high-level view)
    26  
    27  OpenHands emphasizes rigorous, repeatable evaluation across diverse benchmarks and sandboxed environments to ensure agent reliability and safety. 
Example evaluation suites supported in the project include:
    28  
    29  - miniWob
    30  - GPQA
    31  - SWE-Bench
    32  - ML-Bench
    33  - Gorilla
    34  - Logic Reasoning
    35  - Biocoder
    36  - WebArena
    37  - ToolQA and related agent- and model-focused benches
    38  
    39  (These illustrate the breadth of our evaluation program — we run many benchmark suites and simulated environments to ensure readiness for 
real-world public deployments.)
    40  
    41  ---
    42  
    43  ## Roles We Are Hiring
    44  
    45  - Research Scientists (AI / LLMs / agentive systems)
    46  - Applied ML Engineers (model integration, evaluation)
    47  - Software Engineers (backend, frontend, infra)
    48  - Evaluation & Benchmarking Engineers
    49  - DevOps / SRE (deployment and sandboxing)
    50  - Product Managers and Program Leads (public-sector partnerships)
    51  
    52  We welcome applicants who are mission-aligned and excited by public impact.
    53  
    54  ---
    55  
    56  ## Who You Are
    57  
    58  - You care deeply about building AI that is trustworthy and aligned with public values.
    59  - You have a strong background in machine learning, software engineering, or evaluation research.
    60  - You thrive in collaborative, interdisciplinary teams and want to deliver tangible national benefit.
    61  
    62  (We value diverse backgrounds and experiences — if you bring dedication, ethics, and technical excellence, we want to hear from you.)
