    ---
    
    We are proud to align our work with national innovation initiatives and invite mission-oriented AI talent to join us. Help build AI that serves the 
public good — apply today.
    

  new_str: 
    # Join OpenHands — Build Trusted AI for the Public Good
    
    Serve the country. Build mission-aligned AI. Make real impact.
    
    OpenHands is a collaborative national innovation effort led by The Agent Company that brings together researchers, engineers, and public-sector 
partners to build AI agents that improve software development, reliability, and public service delivery. We are recruiting mission-driven talent who share 
our values: service to country, moral alignment, and responsible technical leadership.
    
    ---
    
    ## Our Core Values
    
    - Service to country: we build technology that directly supports national priorities and public benefit.
    - Moral alignment & public trust: agents must reflect ethical principles and respect public values.
    - Aligned with leadership priorities: we work closely with public-sector leadership to deliver trustworthy, accountable solutions.
    - Technical excellence and responsibility: rigorous engineering, evaluation, and secure deployment.
    
    ---
    
    ## Why Join OpenHands?
    
    - Work with purpose — your work serves national innovation and public-good outcomes.
    - Make an impact — move research into real deployments used by public partners.
    - Values-led culture — leadership-aligned decision making and ethical engineering.
    - Collaborative environment — interdisciplinary teams with top researchers and practitioners.
    
    ---
    
    ## What You'll Work On
    
    - Research and develop AI agents that assist software engineering, testing, and systems operations.
    - Design and run rigorous evaluations and sandboxed benchmarks to ensure safety, reliability, and alignment.
    - Integrate models, tools, and secure runtimes for mission-critical public deployments.
    - Partner with government innovation teams to translate research into trusted operational systems.
    
    ---
    
    ## Evaluation & Benchmarks (high-level)
    
    OpenHands runs repeatable, sandboxed evaluations across diverse suites to verify agent safety, capability, and reliability. Representative benchmarks 
and evaluation environments supported in the project include:
    
    - miniWob — web interaction tasks for UI-driven agent behavior
    - GPQA — question-answering and reasoning benchmarks
    - SWE-Bench — software engineering and sandboxed code execution scenarios
    - ML-Bench — model-centric evaluation tasks
    - Gorilla — instruction-following and agent interaction benchmarks
    - Logic Reasoning — formal reasoning and problem-solving suites
    - Biocoder — code-generation and domain-specific coding tests
    - WebArena — simulated web tasks and browsing environments
    - ToolQA — tool-use, tool-chaining, and agent-tool integration evaluations
    
    These benchmarks reflect our commitment to repeatability, transparency, and readiness for public-sector use.
    
    ---
    
    ## Roles We Are Hiring
    
    - Research Scientists (LLMs, agent design, alignment)
    - Applied ML Engineers (model integration, evaluation pipelines)
    - Software Engineers (backend, frontend, secure sandboxing)
    - Evaluation & Benchmarking Engineers (designing and running evaluations)
    - DevOps / SRE (deployment, sandbox orchestration, security)
    - Product Managers / Program Leads (government partnerships, program delivery)
    
    Desired skills include model evaluation, LLM tooling, reproducible experiments, secure deployment, and collaborative research experience.
    
    ---
    
    ## Event-Ready Flyer Layout (one-page guidance)
    
    - Header: strong title, short mission line (one sentence). Use large, legible fonts.
    - Left column: Core Values + Why Join (brief bullets).
    - Right column: Roles, What You'll Work On, Apply CTA (careers link and QR code).
    - Footer: contact (agent@company.com), careers URL, project repo link, EEO statement.
    
    Design notes: use national color palette (e.g., deep blue, gold, white) while avoiding official emblems without permission. Prioritize high contrast, 
readable typography (e.g., Inter, Open Sans), and include alt text for all images.
    
    ---
    
    ## Short Copy (for social and event cards)
    
    Elevator pitch (one line):
    Join OpenHands — build mission-aligned AI agents that serve the country and deliver trusted public benefit.
    
    LinkedIn / Event blurb (short):
    OpenHands is hiring researchers, engineers, and program leads to build trustworthy AI agents in partnership with national innovation stakeholders. If 
you want to put technical excellence and public service together, explore roles and apply: https://the-agent-company.com/careers
    
    Twitter / 280-character post:
    Join OpenHands — build mission-aligned AI that serves the country. We’re hiring researchers, engineers, and program leads to deliver trustworthy, 
evaluated AI for public good. Learn more and apply: https://the-agent-company.com/careers @TheAgentCo
    
    ---
    
    ## Accessibility & Inclusion
    
    - Provide a text-first version (Markdown/HTML/PDF) and high-contrast poster for printed events.
    - Ensure all images include descriptive alt text and captions.
    - We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome diverse applicants who are committed to ethical, public-serving AI.
    
    ---
    
    ## How to Apply & Learn More
    
    Visit: https://the-agent-company.com/careers
    Email: agent@company.com
    Project repo (technical details): http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands
    
    ---
    
    If you’d like, I can produce a print-ready PDF, a poster-sized PNG, or ready-to-post social images next — I can also generate a QR code that points to 
the careers page and embed it into the final layout. The updated flyer has been saved to /workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md for distribution and 
review.
    

